Q: Alternative to set duplicateParentState to true for each child view? A: <p>How about extending the widget -like you said- and overriding <a href="http://developer.android.com/reference/android/view/ViewGroup.html#onLayout(boolean,%20int,%20int,%20int,%20int)" rel="nofollow">onLayout()</a>? This way you ensure to modify the children state also the first time the widget is drawn. When onLayout() is called, getChildCount() will always return the actual number of children. For example:</p>

<pre><code>public class LinearLayout extends android.widget.LinearLayout {

  private static final int[] VIEW_GROUP_ATTRS = new int[]{ android.R.attr.enabled };
  private static final boolean DEFAULT_IS_ENABLED = true;

  private boolean isEnabled = DEFAULT_IS_ENABLED;

  public LinearLayout(Context context) {
    super(context);
  }

  public LinearLayout(Context context, AttributeSet attrs) {
    super(context, attrs);
    isEnabled = context.obtainStyledAttributes(attrs, VIEW_GROUP_ATTRS).getBoolean(0, DEFAULT_IS_ENABLED);
  }


  @Override
  public void setEnabled(boolean enabled) {
    super.setEnabled(enabled);
    this.isEnabled = enabled;

    for (int i = 0; i &lt; getChildCount(); ++i) {
      getChildAt(i).setEnabled(enabled);
    }
  }

  @Override
  protected void onLayout(boolean changed, int left, int top, int right, int bottom) {
    super.onLayout(changed, left, top, right, bottom);
    setEnabled(isEnabled);
  }
}
</code></pre>

<p>Note that you are actually extending the widget (calling super on any method being overridden).</p>
